WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.070
Put algal cells into a solution of an ion,

2
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.690
and keep the outside level constant.

3
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:11.210
Suppose that within 30 minutes, the ion
inside the cells is 10 times as concentrated

4
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.680
as outside.

5
00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:15.210
That is the wrong way for diffusion.

6
00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:19.430
Diffusion alone never builds up
a substance against its gradient.

7
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:24.460
So how can a cell keep taking in a
substance it already holds more of?

8
00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:28.840
In this mission, you'll see how a membrane
protein can move particles from low

9
00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:30.940
concentration to high.

10
00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:36.690
Then you'll look for the 2 tell-tale signs
that set this process apart from diffusion.

11
00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:41.650
Your mission: explain how a cell can keep
taking in a substance it already holds

12
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:42.450
more of.
